#====================================================================
# E2145 - Reconcile downstream references after a canonical package repair
#====================================================================

id:                     E389
trigger_tool:           conan|release|test_package
phase:                  dependency_resolution|publication|validation
error_signature:        Unable to find '.*\.[0-9]+' in remotes|downstream.*temporary version|canonical package.*downstream reference|dependency version mismatch

severity:               2
category:               conan, dependency, publication, validation, versioning
match_keywords:         canonical package reference, temporary repair version, downstream Conan dependency, missing recipe, exact dependency version, package_folder, build never
title:                  Reconcile downstream references after a provider repair keeps the canonical version

root_cause:             A provider repair can replace a broken recipe while retaining the canonical upstream package version and removing a temporary suffixed version. Downstream recipes that were prepared against the temporary reference remain syntactically valid but can never resolve from the official remote, so their release pipeline fails before compilation even though the repaired provider is published.
affected_scope:         Conan dependency chains where a provider correction changes which exact reference is authoritative without changing the upstream software version, especially while downstream recipes are already merged or awaiting release.
verification_cmd:       In a fresh isolated Conan home, download and install the canonical provider with --build=never, prove its RREV/PID/PREV and binary folder, update every downstream recipe and metadata reference, reject the removed reference, then run a consumer test that verifies the exact dependency version and non-null package_folder before compilation.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           canonical-reference-reconciliation
rec_description:        Treat the provider repository and formal binary retrieval as the authority. Replace the obsolete downstream reference in recipe and metadata together, add fail-closed graph checks for the exact canonical version and binary presence, and rerun the complete downstream graph, upstream suite, consumer tests, and current-snapshot target validation.
rec_command:            conan install --requires=<provider>/<canonical-version> -pr:a=<ohos-profile> -r=ohpcd --build=never
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-reference-update-plus-consumer-graph-contract

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      wait-for-authoritative-provider-publication
fallback_description:   If neither reference has a retrievable official binary, preserve local candidates only and wait for the owning provider release. Do not upload a local package or silently build the dependency from source.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       self\.requires\("<provider>/<removed-version>"\)
forbid_1_reason:        A removed or never-published reference cannot be repaired by downstream retries.
forbid_1_consequence:   The downstream release fails at dependency resolution before its build begins.

forbid_2_pattern:       --build=missing|--build=.*provider|conan upload
forbid_2_reason:        Building or uploading the provider from the downstream task bypasses formal publication ownership and can hide the broken reference.
forbid_2_consequence:   Local success is not reproducible by the release worker and may publish an unauthorized binary.

forbid_3_pattern:       version.*check.*only|package_folder.*unchecked|conan list|conan search
forbid_3_reason:        Metadata or version text alone does not prove that the exact target binary is retrievable.
forbid_3_consequence:   A recipe-only or missing-binary provider can pass a superficial check and fail later in CI.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E264]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E2145-draft-2301-dependency-reference-reconciliation.md
last_updated:           2026-08-18
source_event:           libspatialite 5.1.0.2 superseded the merged 5.1.0.1 recipe dependency on removed librttopo 1.1.0.1 with the formally published canonical librttopo 1.1.0

